 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-23", "title": "[dogfood:P1] extractSection cuts a solution body at its first embedded '---' — any corpus answer containing a horizontal rule swallows everything a community editor appends, and import then reports 'skipped: identical content' (silent no-op where an update is expected)", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import"], "notes": "internal/import/git.go:561-577 extractSection(content, '## Solution') returns everything up to the FIRST of \\n---\\n, \\n## , \\n# — but formatSolutionMD (internal/export/git.go:432) writes the stored solution TEXT verbatim, and corpus answers commonly END with a '---' rule inside the body (e.g. producer answer id=2 ends '...coercion (e.g., `\"toString\"` as a key).\\n\\n---'). Byte-proven 2026-09-25: appending 'Update v2' text below that rule yields a parsed solution of exactly the old 830 bytes (simulate-parse + sqlite length comparison), so importAnswer's content-diff sees no change and reports ActionSkipped 'identical content' — the community edit silently vanishes at parse time, before conflict logic could ever fire. Fix direction: cut at the LAST marker, or use a unique sentinel (e.g. a final '<!-- off-by-one:solution-end -->' comment the formatter writes), or parse into a markdown AST. Companion fix: when parsed == stored but the raw FILE bytes differ from the last exported/known bytes, report a parse_warning instead of skipped."}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-24", "title": "[dogfood:P2] POST /api/v1/import accepts conflict_strategy (skip|replace|manual) and returns a 'conflicted' counter — but the field is dropped at handlers.go:970 (never reaches the engine) and the engine has NO conflict/replace/manual code path at all", "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import", "openapi"], "notes": "internal/api/handlers.go:962-970 builds importgit.Config{RepoURL, Branch, LocalDir, SubtreePrefix, GitPath} — ConflictStrategy from the request struct (handlers.go:183) is silently discarded; internal/import/git.go has exactly one Action value for conflict (ActionConflict, git.go:75) and no code that produces it, plus no replace/manual behavior. Live 2026-09-25: skip/replace/manual on identical content all return {skipped:3} identically; nothing distinguishes them. The OpenAPI spec and docs/api-reference.md 'Export / Import' section advertise this parameter. Fix direction: either implement the three strategies or reject unknown/unimplemented values with 400 'not_implemented' — a silently-ignored documented parameter is worse than its absence. Related doc gap: the import response schema has no per-answer details, so operators cannot tell WHAT was skipped; result.Details exists in the engine and is dropped by writeJSON.", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-28 22:28:30.000000", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 22:28:30.000000", "commit_hash": "270459b2", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "PENDING", "worker_summary": "Worker kimi-k3@kimi-for-coding commit 270459b2 (wt/DF-OFF-BY-ONE-24, fast-forwarded to master): Config.ConflictStrategy (skip|replace|manual, \"\" default replace); differing-content branch: skip->ActionSkipped, manual->ActionConflict (counted into res.Conflicted), replace keeps overwrite; handleImport validates (400 invalid_request naming the field) and passes req.ConflictStrategy into the engine; openapi.yaml conflict_strategy default: replace; +194/-6 across 5 files, 3 new tests. Judge tier2 PASS verdict 66e7df07. Covers README-2 (same defect).", "foreman_note": "tick 399: worker 270459b2, judge PASS 66e7df07, guard 4/4. README-2 covered by this fix."}
